A group of order 64 (a 2-group) acting on a set of size 21 must have a fixed point. By the orbit-stabilizer theorem, all orbits under the group action have sizes that are powers of 2. If there were no fixed points, every orbit would have size at least 2, making the total number of elements in the set even. However, 21 is odd, leading to a contradiction. Additionally, the orbit-counting theorem implies the number of fixed points is congruent to 21 mod 2 (i.e., 1 mod 2), so there must be at least one fixed point.

**Final Answer**
\boxed{Yes}

